r18 addition (generic TLS facility):

  79  set_tls_base  rdi = ring-3 GS base   0, or -1 (bad address)

      Anchors the calling task's ring-3 GS base at the given canonical
      low-half address. This is SwirlOS's arch_prctl(ARCH_SET_GS): any
      userland runtime that needs an ELF-style TLS block or an anchored
      thread-info structure (the SwirlRun PE loader's TEB) asks for it
      here. The kernel itself never uses GS, so the value simply stays
      in the MSR; the scheduler re-applies it per task on every switch.

  80  set_user_seg(idx, base, size)   (r20)
      idx 0 = 32-bit code, 1 = 32-bit data/stack (DS/ES/SS), 2 = FS.
      base < 4 GiB, size a multiple of 4096; the whole window must lie in the
      caller's own slot. Returns the ring-3 selector (0x43 / 0x4b / 0x53) or
      -1. The kernel only stores three descriptors per task and reloads
      DS/ES/FS on every return to ring 3; it knows nothing about who uses
      them (userland runtimes use it to run 32-bit code in compatibility mode).
